From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:12:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] turn the camera app into a BLE-only remote control
 (overlay/asteroidos)

The phone side no longer runs the unauthenticated MJPEG/HTTP server, so
asteroid-camera loses the live viewfinder and every network code path.

- Remove camerastreamview.{h,cpp} (QTcpSocket MJPEG/HTTP client) and the
  Qt6::Network dependency; keep Qt6::DBus.
- Add RemoteCameraBridge (remotecamerabridge.{h,cpp}): sendCommand()
  validates against the watch->phone allowlist (capture, flip, zoom_in,
  zoom_out, torch, mode_photo, mode_video, status_query) and calls
  org.asteroidos.btsyncd.AppBridge.sendMessage on the system bus;
  commandReceived() only fires for ready, paused, photo_captured,
  video_started and video_stopped with an empty payload; bleConnected,
  phoneReady and the vibrate helper are exposed to QML.
- main.qml: no video surface; "Waiting for phone camera" until `ready`
  arrives, status_query on start and every 5s until ready, controls
  disabled while the phone is not ready. Status pill, shutter, mode
  toggle, flip, zoom, torch, timer and capture flash are kept.
- camera-companion.patch regenerated with git diff against upstream
  asteroid-camera 53c3e63 and verified to apply to a fresh checkout.
